# `docs/parity-changelog.md` is generated, not written.
#
# It used to be a table every slice appended a row to, marked `merge=union`
# here so git kept both sides instead of raising a conflict. That helped where
# the driver ran - a merge driver is client-side configuration read from this
# file, so a forge performing a merge need not apply it - and it never helped
# with the underlying fact, which is that eight of ten open pull requests were
# editing the same lines of the same file.
#
# Entries now live one per file in `docs/parity-changelog.d/`, so two lanes
# writing at once share no line and there is nothing for a driver to be right
# about. `docs/tools/parity-changelog.py build` renders the published file.
#
# No `merge=union` anywhere, deliberately. It cannot warn about a change that
# is not an append, and nothing here needs it any more.
